[Music]  retired lieutenant general h.r mcmaster  served in the army for 34 years but is  perhaps best known publicly for his 13  months  as president trump's national security  advisor he's been in war zones and gone  head to head with foreign adversaries  mcmasters tells what he learned from all  those experiences in his new book  battlegrounds the fight to defend the  free world and general mcmaster joins  me now from the campus of stanford  university general good morning to you  many people have taken your book and  shaken it upside down hoping dirt falls  out but they have been  unable to find any so i will skip all  that and just cut to the substance an  issue that i know worries you and it  certainly worries me and that is  potential election chaos the fbi is  warning that foreign adversaries may  seek to exploit divisions post-election  and doubt in the process the president  has talked about doubting the process  hillary clinton has  has told joe biden not to concede if  it's messy to you sir  are you worried about what's going to  happen the day after  election day tony first thanks for the  opportunity to be with you  yes i am worried and and the story that  i tell on battlegrounds is is one of how  russia is trying to drag us down right  russia's not that strong  you know they're economies about the  size of texas they have some real  problems and deal with demographics the  collapse of oil prices and so forth and  putin's coming under more and more  pressure but what what putin's trying to  do is he's trying to be kind of the last  man standing and what he wants to do is  polarize us divide us on on the issues  that already divide our society issues  of race and gun control and  and immigration and pit us against each  other and a great way to do that  is to raise doubts about uh about our  our our democratic principles and  institutions and our processes and  especially the election so what do we do  i think for all americans you know we  have  we have to really be cognizant of this  danger tony  how do we how do we temper the situation  which is obviously volatile when you  have russia involved as you say  they are weak but people who are not  weak president trump  former uh secretary of state hillary  clinton they are also commenting on the  election and  fueling the idea that it's going to be  messy and potentially stolen one way or  the other  how do you quiet things when you have  our leaders involved in the fight  well that's a big problem i think all of  our leaders the president everyone you  know  vice president biden everybody i think  has to send a simple clear message to  the american people  that we can secure our election process  and i think tony the american people  ought to be proud of  of what our government has done i mean  under the trump administration  to secure elections after 2016.  as you recall there there's a lot of  progress made between then and 2018  the russians were in many ways foiled in  in in their effort  uh to raise doubts about the 2018  election and to  and to create another crisis of  confidence  some of those reforms involve standing  up new organizations to  you know to protect different  information election infrastructure  but then also our cyber capabilities are  much more agile now we can combine a  good  offense with a good defense but tony i  would just say to you and your  colleagues  i mean what you do as journalists is so  important because we need  authoritative sources of information now  more than ever  and it's in social media and the pseudo  media  where russia kind of has a field day  right they use this  to move us to extremes and and reduce  our confidence in who we are as  americans  yeah well i mean we've been telling  voters to be patient that this could  take some time to count all the votes  but  i'm curious what with your reaction our  job is made more difficult when you have  an exchange like the president had with  a reporter yesterday  he was asked could you commit to a  peaceful transfer of power now that is  conventionally known as a softball  question but the president did not say  of course i commit to that  he instead continued to undermine  confidence in the vote i'm curious  knowing what you know about russia and  foreign actors what was your reaction to  hearing the president say that  well it's one of disappointment i think  we we have to have confidence  in the system that our founders set up  and you know our founders were really  worried about what they called factions  what we now call  political parties and they had very much  in their minds the  the bloody experience of of the english  civil wars in the  in the 17th century and and many of our  founders didn't want parties to exist at  all and so i think it's it's really  important for us to have confidence in  the system they set up  and especially separation of powers  right we do have judicial review and i  know there are these  armies of lawyers from both parties  already out there  but we have to have confidence in the  checks and balances  that our founders set up general  mcmaster one of the remarkable things  about you is in addition to your your  career in the military you also have a  phd  from unc chapel hill and on top of all  that you have an extreme  nonpartisan position you in fact do not  vote sir and have not in your career  i am curious though now that you are  retired will you vote in 2020  well tony i'm having a discussion about  that with my family it's a big change  right i mean i what am i  saying when i was 17 years old you know  and uh  and and so i i really i'm trying to  figure out now you know what my role can  be here in my second  career and and how i'm going to  participate uh in in our democracy  what i really wanted to do with the book  and what i hope i can do in the  discussions  like this after uh you know after its  publication  is to help bring americans together  right as we're at each other's throats  these great challenges to our security  they're they're not going away  and in many ways the crises that we're  encountering today is coveted  general mcmaster has catalyzed catalyzed  these challenges  they're counting me off i will tell  people it's not a juicy read but as one  reviewer said it's a meaty read i will  agree with that  general master thank you very much we  hope you come back very important  conversation  hey thank you so much and the new book  is battlegrounds it is on sale  right now

